    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Imagine a tiny remote-control car "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "racing",
            "ref": "v-race"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a train. Guess who wins? The car—yes, the tiny one! A super-fast "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "model car",
            "zh": "遥控汽车"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " called “The Beast” recently smashed a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "world record",
            "zh": "打破世界纪录"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " by travelling at 234.71 miles per hour. That is almost twice as fast as the quickest trains in the U.K."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "This amazing car was built by an engineer named Stephen Wallis. His love of fast vehicles began when he was a child. “It goes back to when I was eight years old and got my first radio-controlled car,” Stephen said."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "How did he make it? Stephen worked for over a year and used 3D printing to make many of its parts. Interestingly, the car does not have one big engine. Instead, it uses four powerful "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "drone motors",
            "zh": "无人机马达"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to reach high speeds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "One of the biggest challenges was keeping the car on the ground. At such high speeds, even a small "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "bump",
            "zh": "路面颠簸"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " could make the car fly into the sky. So, Stephen had to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "design",
            "ref": "v-design"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " its body carefully to keep the car on the ground."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Finally, he took The Beast to a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "speed event",
            "zh": "速度赛"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in North Wales, where it beat the old record by 16 miles per hour! Stephen won a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Guinness World Record",
            "zh": "吉尼斯世界纪录"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and he also got a special hat as a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "reward",
            "ref": "v-reward"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
